+## Phase 20 - Shade/QS donor audit (user pass 2026-10-22) [ ]
+
+User's visual pass surfaced six issues, concentrated on the shade/QS.
+Each audited against the donor tree
+(~/kitkat-src/frameworks-base/packages/SystemUI) with root cause and
+fix plan below. Fixes are the NEXT work batch.
+
+- [ ] 20.1 Keyboard: missing icon on the numbers-panel toggle key (and
+      the symbol/number flip key in the symbols panel).
+      Root cause: P13 "keyboard-icons-holo (three long-removed icon
+      attrs dropped)" dropped the donor icon attrs that carried these
+      glyphs. Donor: res/xml/kbd_qwerty.xml key_styles
+      latin:keyIconSet / icon keys (sym_keyboard_*_holo_dark mapped
+      via keyIcon attrs). Fix: donor audit of which attrs feed the
+      123/sym toggle keys (keyLabelStyle vs keyIcon), port the donor
+      icon drawables per density into themes-kitkat icon set, and
+      re-add the dropped attr entries. LatinIME tree (pinned fork).
+- [ ] 20.2 Shade drag = modern blur/fade, NOT the donor "unroll".
+      User description (donor behavior): long white bar (the status
+      grab handle) follows the finger; the shade "unrolls" the items
+      as if peeling back to reveal them - i.e. the PANEL TRANSLATES
+      DOWN over an unblurred screen with the handle glued to the
+      drag point; no blur, no alpha fade of content.
+      Root cause A (blur): NotificationShadeDepthController
+      computes shade blur from shadeExpansion whenever SHADE state
+      (shouldApplyShadeBlur) - scrimsVisible only cancels blur when
+      a scrim hits alpha 1 (ScrimController.dispatchScrimsVisible ->
+      OPAQUE), and the 18.5 notification_scrim_transparent=true
+      change zeroed the UNLOCKED scrim alphas, so they NEVER go
+      opaque mid-drag -> blur rides the whole drag. Fix: force
+      shouldApplyShadeBlur() false (or scrimsVisible=true) in SHADE
+      (unlocked) state - keyguard/unlock paths untouched. The modern
+      zoom-out (scale) also rides computeBlurAndZoomOut; force
+      zoomOut 0 in unlocked SHADE.
+      Root cause B (fade vs unroll): the modern shade window fades/
+      alpha-animates the notification STACK as a whole (NSSL
+      alpha/translation on expansion), where the donor PanelView
+      drew the panel's children clipped to mExpandedHeight - the
+      panel "unrolls" because content is CLIPPED from the bottom up,
+      and the 36dp white close handle (status_bar_close 9-patch,
+      NotificationPanelView.draw) is drawn GLUED to the bottom edge
+      of the expanded area, following the finger. Modern NSSL does
+      not clip that way (it scrolls). Fix options: (1) restore the
+      donor PanelView CLIP semantics - NotificationPanelView /
+      NotificationStackScrollLayout with clipChildren + height
+      riding expansion (deep surgery, couples to keyguard swipe);
+      (2) approximate: shade expansion already translates the panel
+      container (full-height translate) - verify the container
+      translate is the active path, kill the content alpha fade
+      (ShadeExpansionStateManager/NSSL alpha animators), and pin the
+      shade_bottom_handle (P3 grabber) to the moving bottom edge so
+      it tracks the finger. DECISION NEEDED from user if (1) vs (2).
+      SCOPE WARNING: same keyguard-coupled area as 18.5; keyguard
+      swipe-up/AOD must stay stock (donor panel never did those).
+- [ ] 20.3 "Manage"/"Clear all" row still visible / looks wrong.
+      Note: 18.3 hid FooterViewModel.manageOrHistoryButton, but the
+      user pass STILL sees footer buttons - the running image predates
+      the 18.3 commit OR the visibility flow does not reach the footer
+      row (FooterViewBinder binds setManageButtonVisible but the
+      footer container itself may stay). ALSO donor truth: 4.4 had
+      NEITHER Manage NOR Clear-all in the shade (clear was the header
+      X, settings was the header gear long-press / settings button;
+      the footer row is a KitKat-era AM/CM feature, not AOSP donor).
+      Fix: verify the 18.3 build landed; then confirm the footer
+      container (notif_footer row) hides entirely (not just buttons)
+      - if the row persists as empty space, GONE the footer container
+      as well. Verify on device.
+- [ ] 20.4 Header clear-all / settings buttons "don't feel right".
+      Donor header (status_bar_expanded_header.xml): clear-all is
+      ic_notify_clear inside ic_notify_button_bg (a dark rounded
+      48x48 press 9-patch), settings button is
+      settings_button_holder FrameLayout (48dp) with
+      ic_sysbar_lamp? no - donor settings_button uses
+      @drawable/ic_notify_settings (a glyph). Modern buttons
+      are: shade_header_clear_all_button (ImageButton with
+      ic_notify_clear donor art, 48dp) and
+      shade_header_settings_button (ic_settings, modern glyph).
+      Audit deltas: settings glyph should be the DONOR
+      ic_notify_settings art (not the modern gear), both buttons
+      need the donor ic_notify_button_bg press background (not
+      selectableItemBackground ripple), and the P3 gear long-press
+      behavior (15.3) reads wrong against the donor (donor settings
+      button is a TAP that opens Settings/flip). DECISION NEEDED:
+      keep the 15.3 tap=flip / long-press=Settings mapping (needed
+      for the two-panel QS flip) but style both buttons donor-faithful
+      (donor glyphs + ic_notify_button_bg backgrounds).
+- [ ] 20.5 Still too much space above the brightness slider.
+      18.4 hid qs_footer and set qs_panel_padding_top 48dp, but the
+      user pass still sees excess. Remaining suspects: (a) the
+      expanded_qs_scroll_view / QSPanel content top padding chain
+      (qs_panel_padding 16dp + tile layout top margin), (b) the QQS
+      header spacer survived (qqs_header height vs qs_header_height
+      both 48dp now?), (c) the media host container reserving space
+      (media controls in QQS per 12.1 note). Fix: measure on device
+      (screencap + geometry walk of the expanded QS) then zero/pin
+      the specific container; re-verify with the same battery.
+- [ ] 20.6 QS tile spacing too wide; panel background not solid black.
+      Donor: quick_settings_cell_gap 4dp, 3 columns (110dp cells),
+      panel background = notification_panel_bg.9.png - a BLACK opaque
+      9-patch (phone bucket), NOT a gradient. Modern tree:
+      qs_tile_margin_horizontal 8dp / vertical 8dp (16dp effective
+      gaps) and rounded_bg_full gradient (P3). Fixes:
+      (a) qs_tile_margin_horizontal/vertical -> 4dp (donor
+      quick_settings_cell_gap), (b) the QS page/panel background:
+      P3 pinned rounded_bg_full to the 4.4 gradient for the SHADE
+      root - donor phone QS page was the flat black 9-patch; either
+      pin the QS container background to #ff000000 (flat) or port
+      notification_panel_bg.9.png as the container bg (donor asset).
+      DECISION NEEDED: gradient vs flat-black for the QS panel vs
+      shade root (donor used BOTH: gradient shade root, flat black
+      QS page after the flip - but 15.3 merged them; pick the
+      donor-faithful pairing: keep gradient shade root, QS page
+      solid black 9-patch).
+
+Cross-cutting: after 20.2/20.3/20.4/20.6 land, re-run the full shade
+battery on the canonical AVD (open/drag/fling feel, header buttons,
+gear/X behavior, QS geometry) before closing any of these.
